===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id=beat}}
From {{der|en|enm|presse||throng, crowd, clothespress}}, partially from {{der|en|ang|press||clothespress}} (from {{der|en|la-med|pressa}}) and from {{der|en|fro|presse|}} (Modern {{cog|fr|presse}}) from {{der|en|fro|presser||to press}}, from {{der|en|la|presso|pressāre}}, from {{m|la|pressus}}, past participle of {{m|la|premo|premere|to press}}.Largely displaced native {{cog|enm|thring||press, crowd, throng}} (from {{cog|ang|þring||a press, crowd, anything that presses or confines}}).
see {{cog|en|thring}}

